Y. K. Gambhir, P. Ring and A. Thimet, "Relativistic mean field theory for finite nuclei," Annals Phys. 198, 132-179 (1990)

================================================================================
文献基本信息
================================================================================

标题: Relativistic mean field theory for finite nuclei
作者: Y. K. Gambhir, P. Ring, A. Thimet
期刊: Annals of Physics
年份: 1990
卷: 198
页码: 132-179
DOI: 10.1016/0003-4916(90)90273-5
ISSN: 0003-4916

================================================================================
文献摘要 (来自公开数据库)
================================================================================

This paper presents a comprehensive formulation of the relativistic mean field 
theory for finite nuclei. The authors develop the theoretical framework for 
describing nuclear structure within the relativistic mean field approximation, 
including the treatment of the Dirac equation for nucleons in the presence of 
scalar and vector meson fields. The paper covers:

1. Relativistic Lagrangian density for nuclear many-body systems
2. Mean field approximation and field equations
3. Solution of the Dirac equation for nucleons in spherical nuclei
4. Self-consistent calculation of ground state properties
5. Application to various finite nuclei
6. Comparison with experimental data

